ledger.proposed_fix:
Do NOT try to make arm() learn the fill (see the separate finding: PlaceOrder cannot return it). Rebase ONCE inside the guard cycle that already holds the number, at zero extra broker cost.

1. Add a `levels_cfg` kwarg to LiveMonitorRegistry.register (backend/app/live/live_position_guard.py:189-207), default None so the manual path and existing tests stay inert. Have backend/app/live_deploy_context.py:146-163 (and backend/app/routers/live_broker.py:370-378) pass the ORIGINAL config -- stop_pct (post-default), stop_pts, target_pct, target_pts, trail. This is required because the registry stores only RESOLVED absolute levels; pct/pts cannot be recovered from them.

2. In LivePositionGuard._cycle, immediately after `entry["seen_filled"] = True` (backend/app/live/live_position_guard.py:723) and BEFORE evaluate_exit (:764), add a one-shot rebase using the `pos` row already in hand at :647:
   - skip if entry.get("entry_fill_rebased") or not entry.get("levels_cfg");
   - fill = _finite_pos(pos.get("daybuyavgprc")) -- the same field/helper already used at :629; skip if None;
   - BLENDED-AVERAGE GUARD: require _parse_netqty(pos.get("daybuyqty")) == entry["qty"]. daybuyavgprc is the day's average across ALL buys of the contract (caveat already recorded in tests/test_live_entry_fill_truth.py:19-23); if the day's buy qty exceeds this position's, it is not this fill. Set entry_fill_rebased=True anyway so it is never retried against a dirtier average;
   - PRISTINE-STATE GUARD: require state["stop_level"] == state["initial_stop"] and not state["activated"], so a rebase can never LOWER a stop trailing has already ratcheted up (the module's stated monotonic invariant, backend/app/live/live_sl_monitor.py:34-35);
   - new = build_monitor_state(fill, **levels_cfg); new["peak"] = max(new["peak"], old["peak"]); entry["state"] = new; entry["entry_price"] = fill; entry["entry_fill_rebased"] = True; log.warning with ref -> fill and old -> new stop.

3. Do NOT re-place the OCO. Verified safe: compute_catastrophe_band keeps the OCO at least MIN_GAP_PP = 15 percentage points below the guard stop (backend/app/live/oco_levels.py:10,43). Rebased guard stop 30.85 vs OCO sl_trigger 21.45 = 9.40 points of headroom, against a basis error bounded by 0.5% + a tick. The ordering can never invert, so the fix stays inside one read path and no background loop has to modify a resting order.

Step 2 also repairs backend/app/live/live_position_guard.py:1259 (basket premium) for free, since it reads entry["entry_price"].
